{
  "tema": 6128,
  "slug": "que-conjuncion-creo-que",
  "titulo": "The conjunction que = that",
  "subtitulo": "«Creo que va a llover.»",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Que links a verb like creer, decir, saber or pensar to the clause that follows (creo que llueve). Unlike English that, it can never be dropped, and it is never pensar de que.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "After verbs of **thinking**, **saying**, **knowing** and **seeing** (**creer, pensar, decir, saber, ver, parecer**…), **que** introduces the next clause."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "Creo",
            "+ que +",
            "va a llover."
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In English, _that_ is often dropped: _I think (that) it'll rain_. In Spanish **que** is **always required**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "No accent: **que** (_that_). **Qué** with an accent is _what_ in questions and exclamations."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Don't add **de**: **pienso que**, **creo que**, **me dijo que** (not **pienso de que**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Short answers: **creo que sí** (_I think so_), **creo que no** (_I don't think so_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **que** is the hitch between two trailers; without it the second one rolls away."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Creo que== va a llover.",
              "en": "I think it's going to rain."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi jefe ==dice que== no hay junta mañana.",
              "en": "My boss says there's no meeting tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Sé que== tienes razón.",
              "en": "I know you're right."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Pienso que== es una buena idea.",
              "en": "I think it's a good idea."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me ==dijo que== estaba cansada.",
              "en": "She told me she was tired."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Veo que== ya terminaste.",
              "en": "I see you've already finished."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Parece que== las olas están grandes hoy.",
              "en": "It looks like the waves are big today."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Vienes a la fiesta? —==Creo que== sí.",
              "en": "Are you coming to the party? —I think so."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
